course: dictionary
lesson: 12983
title: Quick and formal words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Expeditious is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in letters, business and law. It means quick and efficient: something is done fast and without wasting any time. «The council sent an expeditious reply to my letter.» The clues are reply and letter: a reply that arrives fast and sorts things out.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The council sent a quick and efficient reply to my letter» still makes sense, so expeditious must mean quick and efficient.
explain: Watch for the feeling too. In a story, expeditious can make a character sound stiff and official, like a grown-up in a suit. Look out for the phrases «in an expeditious manner» and «expeditious delivery», which both mean done fast.
fact: Expeditious means quick and efficient: done fast and without wasting time.
fact: Expeditious is a formal word, mostly used in letters, business and law.
fact: «An expeditious reply» means a reply that comes quickly and deals with the matter.
fact: «Expeditious delivery» means the parcel arrives fast, with no delay.
fact: A simpler word such as quick can often take its place, but expeditious sounds more official.
exercise: «The council gave an expeditious reply to our letter.» What does expeditious mean here? | Very loud | Lost in the post | Slow and tired | *Quick and efficient
exercise: Which phrase shows something done in a fast, efficient way? | *in an expeditious manner | muddy and wet | sleepy and slow | very, very hidden
exercise: Dad says the bank's expeditious service sorted his card in ten minutes. What does expeditious suggest about the service? | It was cheap and kind | *It was quick and efficient | It was closed for the day | It was slow and muddy
test: «The lawyer sent an expeditious letter about the case.» Which word could replace expeditious without changing the meaning? | Lazy | Hidden | *Prompt | Gloomy
test: Which sentence uses expeditious correctly? | The cat wore an expeditious red hat. | *The team made an expeditious delivery of the parcel. | The sky was expeditious and grey. | She ate an expeditious sandwich, very slowly.
exam: Priya wants to know what expeditious means. Which answer is correct? | *Done quickly and efficiently, without wasting time | Done slowly, with lots of time to spare | Done by a dog | Done in secret, behind a closed door
